  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Labour and Social Security conducted the Integrated Labour Force survey from April 2021 to July 2021. The development of the survey instrument used to collect data for the Labour Force Survey adheres to the Statistical Standards outlined in the 19th International Conference of Labour Statisticians that provides improved definitions for employment and labour underutilization, and also based on the 20th International Conference of Labour Statisticians on work relationships and labour migration. The ILO facilitated training in July 2021 for the Eswatini Statistical Officials regarding the development of the Integrated Labour Force Survey. The training included the design of the survey questionnaire that integrated methodologies and improved definitions of employment and unemployment, as well on new standards on work relationships, as per the 20th International Conference of Labour Statisticians (ICLS).   From August to September 2021, the ILO facilitated training of the Eswatini Statistical Officials focusing on the production of labour migration indicators. During the same training period, the ILO provided capacity support to the Labour Statistical Officials in reviewing labour migration datasets collected in 2016 and 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.1.1. Number of member States that strengthen their labour market statistics, standards and information systems through improved statistical surveys and use of other statistical sources</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
